  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Consultancy for Vocational training, Business training and Mental Health and Psychosocial services under CSIP in Sinjar and Sinuni</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the Iraq Humanitarian Needs Overview, displacement and the COVID-19 pandemic have created barriers to education for over a million IDP and returnee children, while nearly 2 million children require child protection and assistance with gender-based violence. The government&apos;s decision to close the camp compelled IDPs to return to their communities of origin in Sinjar, where basic WASH infrastructure has deteriorated and requires extensive rehabilitation and/or development. The returnee mobility placed an additional strain on the limited infrastructure in Sinjar, Ninewa governorate, which is underserved due to an insufficiency of humanitarian actors and a lack of government ability and commitment. A sizable proportion of IDPs who are unable to return to their country of origin have been forced into secondary displacement.
The project will be delivered directly through joint action between CCR and Cordaid. Based on the input that UNDP will be providing though its other partner, CCR will select the beneficiaries and design market driven VT training courses. CCR and Cordaid will implement VT training, Business training and run One Stop Information and Outreach Center. The distribution of stipends and grants will be done by UNDP&#x2019;s partner with CCR&#x2019;s Support. Based on CCR and Cordaid institutional strength, CCR will oversee the whole project and directly implement Deliverables 1, 2 and 4 which are related to livelihoods and referrals. Cordaid will ensure the implementation of Deliverables 3 and 5 which are related to MHPSS, Gender and Protection. 
CCR will be the focal point for UNDP for reporting and incorporating feedback into the implementation. Deliverables 1 and 2 (vocational training and business management) will be limited to 200 beneficiaries, however,services under Deliverables 3, 4 and 5 will be extended to other community members.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reintegrate economically men and women into the labor force by providing vocational and business development training, small business start-up grants, and psychosocial assistance (PSS) in Sinjar and Sinun.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target 200 men and women where they will obtain Vocational Training, Business Management Training, small business start-up grants and psychological support.</narrative>
  </description>
